# a-core-switched-off — BACKLOG C3, and the control is another file.
#
# ⚠⚠ **This is `a-base-that-plays-its-list.keys` with ONE line added.**
# Same ground, same two towers, same wall with the same gate, same
# four-wave list, same poke, same drive home.  The line is `jammer off`,
# thrown from the core the moment wave 1 is on its way — and the base
# that played four waves plays ONE.
#
# ⚠ That is the whole of C3: the core IS the jammer (`SETTING.md` § The
# recruitment), a wave is *"the gradual accretion of individual cut-off
# robots"*, and a core that is not jamming cuts nobody off.  No list
# advances, so nothing else ever comes.
#
# ⚠⚠ **And it stops the SUPPLY, never the SIEGE.**  Wave 1 is already
# cut off and losing an errand is one way, so the twelve robots already
# walking do not turn round: they arrive, they are fought, and they are
# what the wallet below was spent on.  A switch that emptied the map
# would have retired the SCRAMBLE.
#
# ⚠ The price is in the wallet, and it is not the drain — it is the
# INCOME.  Three waves' worth of bodies were never killed because they
# were never sent, and with the core dark nothing cleared would have
# paid anyway.  `tests/c3_the_jammer.loft` § What the switch is worth is
# the controlled pair; this is the half you can look at.

echo a core switched off: the list stops at one wave and nothing else comes

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
click 1 0
click 1 2
click 1 -2
marker 1 0 tower
marker 1 2 tower

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 18 0
marker 18 0 spawn 3

count markers 5 5
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 20 -2
drag -3 -1 20 -1
drag -3 0 20 0
drag -3 1 20 1
drag -3 2 20 2
count painted 120 120

# The wall, with (6, 0) left open — the gate a crew member can plug.
palette 9
click 6 -2
click 6 -1
click 6 1
click 6 2
kind 6 0 grass
kind 6 1 wall

# ⚠⚠ **`send` PINS THEM, and it is a CONTROL rather than a behaviour**
# (plan 29 O1).  A crew member nobody has told anything now walks to the
# nearest job inside their own senses (3 hexes untrained), so left free
# this one wanders off — and what this file measures is not where the
# crew choose to stand.  ⚠ `helper_drive` is an ORDER the search does not
# overrule (`@X296`), and `send <i> <q> <r>` on the hex they are already
# on is how a fixture says STAY.  ⚠ The free reading is in the comment
# beside the measurement it moves.
crew 6 0
send 0 6 0
helper 0 6 0
roster 1 1
park 0 0

# The mission's list, armed.  Nothing has poked it.
schedule 12 12 12 12
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# ── The poke ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ It has to happen BEFORE the switch: with the core dark nothing is
# being cut off, so there is nothing to provoke and the list would never
# arm at all.  Turning the jammer off is a decision about a run that has
# started.
drive 18 0
tick 10
vehicle 18 0
waves 1 1
count alive 12 12

# ── The drive home, in front of them ────────────────────────────
drive 0 0
tick 10
vehicle 0 0

# ── ⚠⚠ The switch ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One line.  Everything below is what it changes.
jammer off

# ── Wave 1 still arrives, and is still fought ───────────────────
#
# ⚠ The twelve are already cut off, so the switch does nothing for them
# and the base has the same fight it always had.
tick 60
waves 1 1

# ── And nothing else ever comes ─────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ Five hundred ticks.  `a-base-that-plays-its-list.keys` reads
# `waves 4 4` here and finishes with `wallet 20.0 80.0`; this one is
# stuck at one, and the difference is a single line of script.
tick 500
waves 1 1
count alive 0 0
roster 1 1

# ── ⚠⚠ And the price: EXACTLY the two hundred it landed with ────
#
# ⚠ Twelve robots died on this wall and half a metre of one of them is
# still lying at (7, -1) — ten points of salvage, on the ground, with a
# crew member and a vehicle in the base.  Not one point of it can be
# collected, because `jammer_loot_rate` answers 0.0 while the core is
# dark.
#
# ⚠⚠ **The wallet has not moved in either direction**, which is what
# *"a downside on both sides"* looks like from inside a run: nothing
# came for the core, so nothing was drained, and nothing was paid for
# either.  The control finishes at 20-80 having fought four waves and
# been paid for them.
wallet 200.0 200.0
pile 7 -1 0.5 0.5

snap c3_a_core_switched_off
